t.card(t.wo['performance_tasks'][2],'02',cases+' Evaluate the exporter’s opportunity after this movement (7). Evaluate the importer’s position (7).','Case 1: unchanged dollar receipts convert to more Namibia dollars and spare capacity supports a sales response. Benefit depends on buyer response, contracts and other costs, so it is an opportunity rather than guaranteed profit. Case 2: each US$100 input rises N$1,800 to N$2,000; fixed quantity and limited pass-through squeeze the margin. A later substitute or repricing could help, but immediate disadvantage is supported under the stated maintained-peg third-currency conditions.',['Case 1 marks (7): argument for conversion receipts (1), capacity response (1); argument against uncertain buyer response (1), contracts/costs condition (1); condition maintained peg and responsive market (1); judgement opportunity (1), no guaranteed profit (1). Case 2 allocation (7): argument against N$200 higher input (1), limited pass-through squeezes margin (1); limiting argument later substitutes (1), repricing may change outcome (1); condition fixed current quantity/price and peg (1); judgement immediate disadvantage (1), tied to constrained response (1). Total 14.'],[cases])
